
Replication kit for Charles, Hurst, Notowidigdo AMERICAN ECONOMIC REVIEW

For questions/comments, please e-mail noto@alum.mit.edu

To generate the main tables and figures, simply run the following files in order in STATA:



** Build analysis files from Census/ACS
do build.do

** This 
do main.do

** This "flag" runs education analysis for Census/ACS
do main.do "education"

** This file runs all of the analysis of IPEDS
cd ipeds
do ipeds_main.do
cd ../

** General additional graphs
do main.do "graphs"




After these files have been run, the tables will be in numbered "txt"
files in "output" folder, and the figures will be numbered "eps" and
"pdf" files in the same folder.



The NLSY analysis uses restricted-use geo-coded data. The code for
this analysis is given in "nlsy" folder, but to get access to the data
to run this code, visit this website for more details:
https://nlsy97.norc.org/ or contact Matt Notowidigdo at e-mail above
for assistance in getting access to the restricted-use data.